# Line-ending policy.
#
# The build and several contract tests compare exact byte counts and literal
# source fragments, and `git apply` matches patch context bytes literally. With
# core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) a fresh checkout rewrites every text
# artifact to CRLF, which silently breaks all of that:
#
#   offline_translation/llama.cpp-LICENSE.txt   1078 -> 1099 bytes (21 lines)
#   vendor patch files                          268,931 -> 274,366 bytes
#
# Pin the working tree to LF on every platform and normalise on commit, so a
# checkout is byte-identical to the stored blob regardless of the machine's
# autocrlf setting. Binary files are auto-detected and left untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Patch files must never be converted at all: `-text` opts them out of both the
# checkout conversion and commit normalisation.
*.patch -text
third_party/patches/*.patch whitespace=-blank-at-eol
